{"agent":"impl-ra-t3-chat","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"budget_forced":"post-rebase onto main 1350 commits; try the new gemini reviewer; prior budget spent","chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"`chat_t3` only returns true when `cfg.sources.get(\"approvals.accept_chat_for_t3\") == \"local\"`. The operator decision D-RA-T3-chat only requires the opt-in to be on; it does not say the opt-in is limited to `.ddflow/local/config.toml`, and the config system demonstrably supports environment-delivered approval knobs (`DDFLOW_APPROVALS_FORBID_CHAT_FOR_T3` is checked in `_forbidden`). Given `DDFLOW_APPROVALS_ACCEPT_CHAT_FOR_T3=true` with no local file, `cfg.approvals.accept_chat_for_t3` is true but the source is not `\"local\"`, so `chat_t3` returns False and a typed T3 attestation that D-RA-T3-chat says should be accepted is rejected.","digest":"f2272c7cffd2ea8a","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:chat_t3","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:chat_t3"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"When `_gate_problem(prev, text)` is falsy, the new operand constructs `KeyRefused(AG.problem(_parsed(prev), _parsed(text)))` unconditionally. For an edit with no approvals problem, `AG.problem(...)` returns `None`, so this expression evaluates to a truthy `KeyRefused(None)` instance (Python objects are truthy unless a custom `__bool__` is defined, and this change does not add one). The surrounding `or` therefore returns that empty refusal object immediately, making the later `_human_removed` and `_workflow_refusal` checks unreachable. Input: a config edit that needs a workflow/human-removed refusal but has no approvals guard problem; line 809 stops before those guards and refuses the edit with no message.","digest":"e37f77d4a7f4545d","location":"ddflow/services/configwrite.py:809 KeyRefused(AG.problem(...))","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/configwrite.py:809 KeyRefused(AG.problem(...))"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"`new = 'false'` is the TOML string `\"false\"`, not the boolean `false` (which must be written without quotes). The key `approvals.forbid_chat_for_t3` is a boolean config option whose default is meant to be off. When this `knob_added` record is folded into a release and consumed by the upgrade/configwrite path, it carries a string where a bool is required: either the config parser rejects the wrong type, or a non-empty string `\"false\"` is truthy and the default becomes effectively “forbid on,” silently forbidding all typed T3 chat.","digest":"c7abdd70f1e62b2d","location":"ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.approvals.forbid_chat_for_t3.toml:6","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/templates/upgrade/unreleased/knob_added.approvals.forbid_chat_for_t3.toml:6"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"The autouse fixture clears only `DDFLOW_AGENT` and `AP.HARNESS_MARKERS`, but does not clear the new approval-knob environment variables. A test process with `DDFLOW_APPROVALS_FORBID_CHAT_FOR_T3=true` exported (the same variable `test_the_environment_can_forbid` relies on) will make `test_a_typed_answer_approves_a_t3_act_and_is_graded` fail: `_cfg` creates a config with `forbid_chat_for_t3=False`, but `H.attest`/`H.chat_t3` sees the environment's forbid and refuses the approval, so the test's `assert ok, message` fails. The fixture should clear `DDFLOW_APPROVALS_FORBID_CHAT_FOR_T3` (and `DDFLOW_APPROVALS_ACCEPT_CHAT_FOR_T3`) to make the tests hermetic.","digest":"4eff86a9b091d5c6","location":"tests/test_approvals_t3_chat.py:_a_person","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_approvals_t3_chat.py:_a_person"}],"chunks_total":7,"coverage":"7/7 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":4,"diff_chars":36485,"diff_sha":"b085144554068dd92a989864505f3756d0382e1e4ea014c9714da711bc72d4bf","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1303.4,"excluded_bytes":1424082,"excluded_files":3,"excluded_paths